    "cardType": "FACT",
    "front": "Does $f^{-1}(x)$ mean $\\frac{1}{f(x)}$?",
    "back": "No. The $-1$ means “inverse function”, not a reciprocal.",
    "notes": "For $f(x) = x^5$: $f^{-1}(x) = \\sqrt[5]{x}$, not $\\frac{1}{x^5}$.",
    "concepts": [
      "math.algebra.inverse-and-composite-functions"
    ]
